1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:07,400
This is Placement OS, a demo build with fictional data.

2
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:13,500
I will walk through what a student does,

3
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:19,200
then what a placement officer does.

4
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:26,000
Here is the profile: academics, contact, links, skills and preferences.

5
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:32,000
The meter shows percentage done and the next step.

6
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:37,300
The checklist marks each item Done or To do.

7
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:46,000
Each academic field has a status: not verified yet, self-reported, or verified.

8
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:54,000
The placement cell checks these manually.

9
00:00:55,400 --> 00:01:04,000
I can save up to five resume links, with labels,

10
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:14,000
and mark one as default.

11
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:24,500
The Opportunities tab lists drives. I can search by company or role.

12
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:34,300
Saved keeps drives for later. Packages show in lakh per annum.

13
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:44,000
I can filter by eligibility and by status, such as open or closing soon.

14
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:53,300
And sort by closing first, newest or highest pay.

15
00:01:55,400 --> 00:02:02,000
Open a drive and you see the role, rounds, requirements and deadline.

16
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:08,800
Compensation shows in LPA, with a live countdown.

17
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:17,000
The eligibility card shows what is required and what my profile says.

18
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:24,200
If a detail is missing, it shows Check profile instead.

19
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:31,500
Tap Opt in. Before anything is sent, I see a review.

20
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:38,300
Each prefilled field shows its source and verification status.

21
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:45,000
I choose a resume. Only questions my profile cannot answer are asked.

22
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:50,800
Conflicts and missing details are flagged before I can submit.

23
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:58,000
I accept the declaration and submit.

24
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:03,800
Nothing is sent until I do.

25
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:11,600
I get a reference number.

26
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:17,800
The application has a timeline. Until screening starts, I can withdraw.

27
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:23,700
In Settings: reminders at 60, 30 and 15 minutes.

28
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:29,300
Quiet hours pause push. In-app still delivers.

29
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:39,000
Now the officer view. The dashboard shows open drives,

30
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:49,300
drives closing today, applications today and pending verifications.

31
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:57,000
To create a drive I use the wizard: company, role, description and compensation.

32
00:03:57,200 --> 00:04:04,300
Nine steps. It autosaves as a draft.

33
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:18,800
Eligibility rules: minimum CGPA, backlogs, allowed departments and batches.

34
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:33,800
Then custom questions and the selection rounds.

35
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:48,800
And the timeline: deadline, contact and a policy note.

36
00:04:50,400 --> 00:05:01,800
Before publishing, a completeness check lists anything missing.

37
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:09,000
Who can apply: the eligible count, with reasons.

38
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:14,300
Blocked students are counted per rule.

39
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:21,500
After publishing, applicants appear.

40
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:27,000
I filter by status and open any student.

41
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:34,000
Stages: screening, assessment, interview, selected, offer, joined.

42
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:39,300
Only allowed next steps are shown. Every change is recorded.

43
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:46,500
I can send an announcement to everyone

44
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:51,400
or to one drive's participants.

45
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:59,400
That is the walkthrough. Launching soon with a campus pilot. Link below.

